            <ArticleTitle>[Immediate analgesic effects of tendon acupuncture on soft tissue injury].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>927-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To observe the immediate analgesic effect of tendon acupuncture on soft tissue injury in different sites.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A total of 140 cases of soft tissue injury, involving 14 injury sites, were treated with tendon acupuncture. According to the principle of &quot;considering pain as acupoint&quot;, based on injury sites, one to three tendon acupoints were selected in each tendon, which were treated with 1 to 5 times. Totally 676 times Of treatment was given. The visual analogue scale (VAS) was used to evaluate the immediate. analgesic effect before and after the treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">After the treatment, the score of VAS was significantly reduced (4. 20+ 1. 77 vs 2. 43 ± 1. 30, P&lt;0. 001); regardless of the total number of treatment, the score of VAS after each acupuncture was obviously reduced compared with that before acupuncture (all P&lt;0. 001); the score of VAS at each injury sites after treatment was significantly reduced compared with that before treatment (all P&lt;0. 001).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">There is an immediate analgesic effect of tendon acupuncture for different sites of soft tissue injury. Also, the effect has been shown in different frequencies of treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
